# Copy to .env.local and edit only if you need to override the default.
#
# You usually do NOT need this file: `make dev` sets EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL from
# your current LAN IP automatically, which is what a physical device needs.
# Set it here only to pin a specific host.
#
#   local API over LAN   http://192.168.2.40:3000/api
#   simulator only       http://localhost:3000/api
#   production           https://api.fridgie.ca/api
#
# The websocket URL is derived from this by swapping http → ws, so it must
# include the /api suffix and must not be a trailing-slash URL.

# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.2.40:3000/api

# Fridgie Pro uses RevenueCat's public, platform-specific SDK keys. These are
# safe in a client build; the REVENUECAT_SECRET_API_KEY is server-only and must
# never be placed here. Checkout stays disabled until the active platform key
# and both HTTPS legal links are configured.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_REVENUECAT_IOS_API_KEY=appl_...
# EXPO_PUBLIC_REVENUECAT_ANDROID_API_KEY=goog_...
# EXPO_PUBLIC_REVENUECAT_PRO_ENTITLEMENT_ID=fridgie_pro
# EXPO_PUBLIC_REVENUECAT_OFFERING_ID=default
# EXPO_PUBLIC_FRIDGIE_PRO_MONTHLY_PRODUCT_ID=fridgie_pro_monthly
# EXPO_PUBLIC_FRIDGIE_PRO_ANNUAL_PRODUCT_ID=fridgie_pro_annual
# EXPO_PUBLIC_PRIVACY_URL=https://fridgie.example/privacy
# EXPO_PUBLIC_TERMS_URL=https://fridgie.example/terms
